[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) is marked known: one parser bug, one fix queued. Read the reports instead
of the subject lines and it holds three problems. The queued parser fix closes only one of them.

<Callout kind="warn">
Do not close #4471 when the parser fix ships. The other two problems keep coming in.
</Callout>

## The split

<ProblemSplit ticket={4471} links={{
  parser: 'https://github.com/nmorel/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/1',
  hint: 'https://github.com/nmorel/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/2',
  'one-day': 'https://github.com/nmorel/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/3',
}} />

Counts are of unique reports. The export pages overlap, so some reports appear twice in
`reports-4471.json`; each id counts once.

## How each report was placed

- **`parser`**: the shared parser reads every date month first, and every tenant on file writes
  the day first. A booking for 4 March comes out as 3 April. Reports by app and email, and by form
  from booking-v2 tenants.
- **`hint`**: booking-v3 prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field. People at day-first tenants
  (Alder Physio, Copper Studio, Pale Harbour) type what the hint says, and the form reads it the
  tenant's way. The result looks like the parser bug, but the parser fix does not touch it: the
  hint has to change.
- **`one-day`**: the date moves by one day and the month stays right ("Tuesday 12 May, calendar
  says Monday 11 May"; Lisbon got Tuesday, Toronto got Monday). That is not a swapped month, so it
  is a time-zone or date-boundary bug. The desk already listed these in `desk-notes.json`, but
  CauseTable counts them under `parser` and only footnotes them.

## Why #4471 looked like one problem

- The desk merges on subject line alone ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)). All
  three problems arrive as "Date is wrong" or "Booking on the wrong date".
- Intake's tag is a guess from the reporter's browser locale, not from the tenant. The "intake tag
  agrees" column shows how often it is right.
- CauseTable groups by tenant and channel only, so a one-day move lands under `parser`.

## What to do

1. Keep the parser fix on #4471's queue: it covers the `parser` row.
2. Change booking-v3's hint to the tenant's own date order, or make the form follow its hint.
3. Look for the one-day move in time-zone handling: where an invite turns a local date into a time
   and back.
4. When you merge a date report, read the body and place it with the tenant's locale and form,
   not with its subject or intake tag.

